cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GLiNER2.5-Decide playground: fast local decisions, from ticket routing to a Space Invaders copilot"
message: "If you use this code, please cite the repository and, above all, the GLiNER2 paper it builds on."
type: software
authors:
  # CFF requires a person (family-names) or an entity (name).
  # An entity entry keeps the citation valid without a legal name.
  - name: "wiseright"
    alias: "wiseright"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wiseright/gliner-decide-playground"
abstract: >-
  Companion code for a Medium article on decision models. Six applied examples
  of GLiNER2.5-Decide, a like-for-like end-to-end latency benchmark against
  4-bit quantised Qwen models on a single Colab T4, and two Space Invaders
  experiments that put a 340M encoder inside a 50 ms real-time loop.
keywords:
  - decision-models
  - gliner
  - text-classification
  - zero-shot-classification
  - latency-benchmark
  - atari
  - gymnasium
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-26"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "GLiNER2: An Efficient Multi-Task Information Extraction System with Schema-Driven Interface"
    authors:
      - name: "Fastino AI and contributors"
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2507.18546"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.18546"
  - type: article
    title: "GLiNER: Generalist Model for Named Entity Recognition using Bidirectional Transformer"
    authors:
      - family-names: Zaratiana
        given-names: Urchade
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2311.08526"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.08526"
  - type: software
    title: "GLiNER2.5-Decide"
    authors:
      - name: "Fastino AI"
    url: "https://huggingface.co/fastino/GLiNER2.5-Decide"
